---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site, localBusinessSchema } from '../../config/site';

const procedureSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "MedicalProcedure",
  "name": "Sedation Dentistry",
  "description": "Lose your fear of treatment with stress-free sedation dentistry in Houston, TX.",
  "procedureType": "https://schema.org/Therapeutic",
  "provider": {
    "@type": "Dentist",
    "name": "Dentiq Dentistry",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "Houston"
    }
  }
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Sedation Dentistry Houston | ${site.name}`}
  description="Lose your fear of treatment with stress-free sedation dentistry in Houston, TX."
  schema={[localBusinessSchema, procedureSchema]}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-primary mb-4">
      <a href="/services" class="hover:underline">Services</a>
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-4 leading-tight">
      Sedation Dentistry
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-neutral-mid mb-8 leading-relaxed">
      Lose your fear of treatment with stress-free sedation dentistry in Houston, TX.
    </p>
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-neutral-mid leading-relaxed">
      <p class="mb-4">Sedation dentistry, sometimes called Sleep Dentistry, is a safe, gentle option used to help patients relax while having dental treatment. Medication is used, but you usually remain awake unless you opt for general anesthesia. Dentiq offers both nitrous oxide and IV sedation depending on the procedure and your comfort level. If the thought of dental treatment fills you with dread — whether due to a phobia, low pain threshold, sensitive gag reflex, or a large amount of work needed — sedation dentistry makes it possible to complete treatment comfortably and efficiently.</p>
      
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
      <a href="/schedule" class="btn-primary">Ask About Sedation Options</a>
      <a href="/services" class="btn-secondary">View All Services</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-16 md:pb-24">
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-neutral-mid leading-relaxed space-y-4">
      <p>Sedation dentistry, sometimes called 'Sleep Dentistry,' is a safe, gentle option used to help patients relax while having dental treatment</p>
      <p>Medication is used, but patients usually remain awake unless they opt for a general anesthetic</p>
      <p>Available sedation options include local anesthesia, nitrous oxide, sedation anesthesia (IV), and general anesthesia</p>
      <p>Local anesthesia is an anesthetic applied directly to the area of removal</p>
      <p>Sedation anesthesia is administered through an intravenous (IV) line</p>
      <p>General anesthesia is an anesthetic delivered to allow a deep sleep during the procedure</p>
      <p>Suitable for patients with a fear of dentists, low pain threshold, very sensitive teeth, a gag reflex, or a need for a vast amount of work</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
